      "data": {
        "value": "<p><strong><u>Custom IHC Panel</u></strong><br><br><strong>IHC No-&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;85/24</strong><br><strong>Gross :-&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Received &nbsp;block No. B/65625/24<br><strong>Microscopic Exam : Mild chronic active proctitis</strong><br><br><strong>IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY</strong></p>\n<table class=\"cke_show_border\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&nbsp;IHC</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Immunoreactivity</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CMV&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; NON-IMMUNOREACTIVE-&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Negative&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Comments : Muld chronic active proctitis</strong><br>&nbsp;<strong>Notes :</strong><br>&nbsp;1.&nbsp;This test was performed on paraffin embedded tissue section.<br>2.&nbsp;Detection system used &ndash; Biogenex &nbsp;Real Envision Detection system, peroxidase/ DAB + Rabbit/mouse.<br>3.&nbsp;The impression is based on the material submitted and is not a complete surgical pathlogy report.<br>4.&nbsp;Improper Fixation may affect results.&nbsp;<br>5.&nbsp;This assay has not been validated on decalified tissue. Results should be interpreted with caution given the likelihood or false negativity of decalcified specimen.<br>&nbsp;<strong>Fixative requirement :</strong><br>&nbsp;1.&nbsp;The volume of formalin fixative should be atleast 10 times the volume of the specimen<br>2.&nbsp;Specimens should be immersed in 10% neutral buffered formalin within 1 hours of the biopsy/ resection procedure ( time of removal&nbsp;and time of immersion to be mentioned )<br>3. In all resection (large) specimens , the tumour must be bisected prior to immersion in fixative.</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
      "_id": "676e687d0a16e71b7d79bce5"
    }
